<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM shares firm after Merrill upgrade.</title>
<headline>KLM shares firm after Merrill upgrade.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in flag carrier KLM Royal Dutch Airlines rose 2.20 guilders or 4.1 percent to 56.00 guilders early on Monday in continued buying linked to a U.S. broker upgrade.</p>
<p>On Friday brokerage Merrill Lynch said it had upgraded the airline to a near-, long-term buy from accumulate.</p>
<p>No further details were given.</p>
<p>Dealers in Amsterdam attributed the buying to local demand, sparked by news of the upgrade. The rest of the bourse was slightly firmer, the AEX up 0.60 points at 677.28.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
